v {xschem version=3.4.8RC file_version=1.2
*
* A net label for the implicit body ties inside the mosbius_* device
* subcircuits. Identical to devices/lab_pin.sym -- same type=label, same
* "*.alias @lab" format, so it netlists to the same comment line and
* names the net the same way -- except its pin is dir=inout rather than
* dir=in.
*
* That one attribute is the whole point. The body net is a port of the
* subcircuit (supplied by the device symbol's `extra` attribute, so it
* never appears on the schematic), but the only other thing on the net
* is the sky130 FET's B terminal, which is dir=in. Two `in` pins and no
* driver makes xschem's connectivity check report
*
*     Error: undriven node: b
*
* on every GUI netlist. A real iopin would silence that, but then the
* schematic declares a pin the symbol does not have, and the pin-count
* check fails instead. type=label keeps it out of the port list; dir=inout
* makes it count as a driver. Both checks pass, netlist unchanged.
}
G {}
K {type=label
format="*.alias @lab"
template="name=p1 lab=b"
}
V {}
S {}
E {}
B 5 -1.25 -1.25 1.25 1.25 {name=p dir=inout}
L 4 -10 0 10 0 {}
L 4 -6 5 6 5 {}
L 4 -2 10 2 10 {}
T {@lab} -7.5 -18 0 0 0.3 0.3 {}
